      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is the host even expected to call `enable_virtualization_cpu` more than once for the same CPU? It doesn\u0027t seem so: looks like that only happens if kvm-intel.ko is unloaded and loaded again (while pKVM doesn\u0027t support building KVM as a module) or during S3 resume (which is not supported by pKVM either).\n\nSo we should rather add a more generic per-cpu variable e.g. `virtualization_enabled` (BTW like the one in virt/kvm/kvm_main.c) and immediately return from `pkvm_enable_virtualization_cpu()` (with e.g. -EBUSY) if it is called more than once for the same CPU? In particular, to prevent similar security issues if we add more logic to `pkvm_enable_virtualization_cpu()` in the future.",
      "fixSuggestions": [
        {
          "fixId": "afa6bd0d_6df0826b",
          "description": "prompt_to_edit API",
